# Handwritten Digit Recognition

A handwritten digit recognition web application built using **Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN)**, TensorFlow, and Streamlit.

## Project Overview

This project recognizes handwritten digits (0–9) drawn by users on an interactive canvas. A trained CNN model processes the drawing and predicts the digit with a confidence score.

## Features

- Interactive drawing canvas
- Real-time digit prediction
- Prediction confidence scores
- Probability visualization for all 10 digits
- Processed image preview

## Model Performance

- Dataset: MNIST
- Training images: 60,000
- Testing images: 10,000
- Image dimensions: 28 × 28 pixels
- Test accuracy: **99.1%**

*Accuracy is measured on the MNIST test dataset.*

## Technologies Used

- Python
- TensorFlow / Keras
- NumPy
- OpenCV
- Streamlit
- Streamlit Drawable Canvas

## Project Structure

```text
handwritten-digit-recognition/
├── app.py
├── digit_recognition_model.keras
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

## Run Locally

1. Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/vtu25590-bot/handwritten-digit-recognition.git
cd handwritten-digit-recognition
```

2. Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

3. Start the application:

```bash
streamlit run app.py
```

